note How one command line becomes a Command and runs. The process arguments after the root and the GUI output panel's input line both go through cli::parse, which is clap over the Command enum, so help and argument errors read the same in both. exec runs the parsed command against the index and map and says whether the map changed; the CLI saves and exits, the GUI marks the map dirty and leaves saving to ctrl+s. The two front ends share everything but the argument splitting, which the shell does for the CLI.

