note Parse before indexing so a usage error costs nothing. Then build the index from the cache and tree-sitter, and hand exec a Servers, which starts a language server only when the command needs one. Help goes to stdout with exit 0, usage errors to stderr with exit 2. A map that does not read stops the command with exit 2, before anything could save over it. A mutating command saves the map. A command error prints what it produced so far and exits 2; check relies on this. Output goes through emit so a closed pipe does not panic.

